<Layout
  title="About Me | Penny Xu"
  description="Penny Xu — systems engineer in the Bay Area working on GPU and graphics systems at Apple, currently going deep on LLM inference."
>
  <h1>About Me</h1>
  <p>
    I'm a systems engineer in the Bay Area. I work on GPU and graphics systems
    at Apple — screen capture, display pipelines, the layer where software
    finally meets the hardware — and before that, the Vulkan driver stack at
    Samsung. Computer Engineering at UIUC, with a semester at EPFL.
  </p>
  <p>
    Lately I've been deep in LLM inference: how these models actually get
    served, where all the memory goes, and why serving them turns out to be an
    operating systems problem wearing a machine learning hat. It's the most fun
    I've had with a technical problem in years, and it's where I'm headed next.
  </p>
  <p>
    I write here to understand things properly. If an idea won't fit in my
    head, I draw it until it does.
  </p>
  <p>
    Outside of that: tennis, skiing, motorcycles. Also challenge me in chess!
